# Auto-publishing Monomi's OWN content-calendar posts to Instagram + the
# Facebook Page (optional). Leave all three empty to keep it off (the app boots;
# the calendar shows "not configured"). Phase 1 publishes for the internal
# client (Monomi) only. Setup in Meta Business Settings:
#  1. Users > System users: create an Admin (or Employee) system user.
#  2. Assign assets to it: the Monomi Facebook Page (with "Content" / create
#     content access) and the Instagram account linked to that Page, and add
#     the Meta app the token is generated for (Apps > Add assets).
#  3. Generate token (never-expiring) with: pages_show_list,
#     pages_read_engagement, pages_manage_posts, instagram_basic,
#     instagram_content_publish, business_management.
#  4. META_PAGE_ID = numeric Page id; META_IG_USER_ID = the Page's
#     instagram_business_account.id (the calendar's "Check connection" shows it).
# The token is read from the environment only: never stored, logged or
# returned by the API. Graph version is shared with META_GRAPH_VERSION.
META_SYSTEM_USER_TOKEN=
META_PAGE_ID=
META_IG_USER_ID=
# Optional: app secret of the app that owns the token -> appsecret_proof on every call
META_SYSTEM_APP_SECRET=
# Optional kill switch for the every-minute auto-publish job (true/false)
META_AUTOPUBLISH_ENABLED=true
# Dev only (ignored in production): fake Graph server for graph/graph-video/rupload
# META_GRAPH_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5499
